# Abadi's Private Authentication protocol (PrivAuth), running example of the paper.
#
#   1. A -> B : {A, NA}pubk(B)
#   2. C -> A : {C, NA, NC}pubk(A)        (if beta)
#   2'. C -> A : {N}K                     (decoy, if not beta)
#
# In Phoebe the roles are A (initiator) and C (responder); the responder role C
# performs the receive of step 1, while `B` is only the principal the message is
# encrypted to.  Hence the arrows below go A -> C and C -> A, and `B` appears
# inside the message term.  `phi` is the responder's enabling test (named beta
# in the paper).

protocol PrivAuth
roles   A C
names   B
nonces  NA NC N
keys    KK

1. A -> C : { < A, NA > }_B              ; new NA
2. C -> A : { < C, NA, NC > }_A          ; new NC ; send_test phi
 | C -> A : {| N |}_KK                    ; new N, KK
